------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Presentations of groups
--
-- The windows of the five-wire derivations, as records
--
-- The derivations of Five.D take their windows as an argument (see
-- `scratchpad/five/winlib5.py`): `WsL` holds the literal windows and
-- the two-wire equations of Five.D.TR, `Ws` the literal ones (`lit`)
-- and the placed ones.  Each window is a function of the record, of
-- its own name; the records themselves hold chunks of at most
-- 100 windows (`WsL01`, …, `Ws01`, …), since a record costs the
-- square of its number of fields.  Five.WinInstL and Five.WinInst
-- build them.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

